    "title": "Where is Queens University? Basketball coach wears sweaters in March Madness",
    "text": "PURDUEWhere is Queens University? What to know about Purdue basketball March Madness opponent Aaron FergusonIndianapolis StarUpdated March 20, 2026, 8:16 p.m. ETQueens University is making its first appearance in the NCAA Tournament, and hopes to become the latest double-digit seed to beat Purdue basketball in the big dance.The Royals (21-13) are a fun group, some might say the best March Madness story in the bracket. Their coach, Grant Leonard, wears sweaters on the sideline that have certainly drawn the attention with a few viral moments. They have a ceramic dog, Buddy, the players say is their identity — don't get it mixed up with mascot. They also were founded as an all-girls school, becoming an all-girls seminary, before allowing co-eds in the late 1980s.Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
